           2014 Contributor.
License: Apache-2.0
Comment:
 The holder spellings above are the ones used in the source headers. A few
 test files say "Copyright (c) 2014 Contributor." with no licence of their
 own; they were contributed to the Scala project under its Apache-2.0
 licence and contributor agreement. The CompletionLatch class in
 src/library/scala/concurrent/impl/Promise.scala says it is inspired by
 Doug Lea's public domain AbstractQueuedSynchronizer; the file itself is
 under the Scala header. The files marked "imported from
 scalamacros/paradise" come from the macro paradise plugin, whose only
 holder is EPFL (BSD-3-clause, "Copyright (c) 2013-2015 EPFL"); EPFL
 contributed them to Scala under Apache-2.0.

Files: src/reflect/scala/reflect/internal/util/AlmostFinalValue.java
Copyright: EPFL and Lightbend, Inc. dba Akka
           Remi Forax
License: Apache-2.0
Comment:
 The file says it is "Originally from the JSR-292 cookbook created by Remi
 Forax" (the jsr292-cookbook project on the now closed Google Code,
 published under the New BSD licence) and was since reworked by the Scala
 team. Its
 header is the Scala Apache-2.0 one; the original author is listed here.

Files: src/library/scala/math/BigInt.scala
Copyright: EPFL and Lightbend, Inc. dba Akka
           2011 The Guava Authors
